  "details": "Issue #1: Group Cloning;\nWhen using Udon and Hotkeys such as Ctrl C, V and Z, you will find that all groups may get cloned. This is discovered by moving groups. If you delete these groups, there is a chance that the group you deleted was not a clone, leaving you with a full Udon Graph until you save or use Ctrl Z, all the items within the clones will disappear and your graph is now destroyed, unless you Ctrl Z all the way back to before the group cloning occured.\nIssue #2: Comments;\nMade a comment card in the Udon Graph, it disappeared without a trace.",
